severe clinical events, defined as death or hospital admission irrespective of the cause. Analyses were by intention to 
treat. FINDINGS Four of the randomised patients were excluded (positive for HIV-2 only). 120 severe events occurred 
among 271 patients in the co-trimoxazole group and 198 among 270 in the placebo group. Significantly fewer patients in 
the co-trimoxazole group than in the placebo group had at least one severe event (84 vs 124); the probability of 
remaining free of severe events was 63.7% versus 45.8% (hazard ratio 0.57 [95% CI 0.43-0.75], p=0.0001) and the benefit 
