uninfected children. RESULTS Overall, 808 children (190 HIV-infected, 499 HIV-uninfected but born to infected mothers, 
and 119 born to HIV-uninfected mothers) were included in this study. Of these, 109 died during a median follow-up of 18 
months. Rates of childhood immunizations were high among all children (eg, lowest was measles vaccination [87%] among 
HIV-infected children). Age-adjusted morbidity rates were significantly higher among HIV-infected than among 
HIV-uninfected children. HIV-infected children were more immunosuppressed than were uninfected children. By 3 years of 
